course: dictionary
lesson: 286
title: Among, the word for "in the middle of"
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Among is a small word that tells you where something is or who it belongs with. It can mean in the middle of a group, as in «a house among the trees», where the house is surrounded by trees.
explain: Among can also mean shared out between people. «Shared equally among three friends» means the sweets are divided into three equal parts, one for each friend.
explain: Among can mean being one of a group. «Parrots are among the cleverest birds» means parrots are in the group of clever birds. To check, swap in the words «one of» or «in the middle of» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Among means in the middle of a group, shared with each person of a group, or being one of a group.
fact: Among is a preposition: it links a noun to the rest of the sentence, as in «among the trees».
fact: «Shared among three friends» means divided by 3, so each friend gets an equal share.
fact: «Parrots are among the cleverest birds» means parrots are one of the cleverest birds.
fact: The harvest mouse weaves a ball-shaped nest among tall grass or wheat stalks.
exercise: «The harvest mouse weaves a ball-shaped nest among tall grass.» Where is the nest? | Far away from any plants | *In the middle of the tall grass | Inside a box | Under the sea
exercise: Mum shared the cake among the three of us. What does among mean here? | Hidden under the plate | Being one of the cake | *Shared with each person, so each gets a part | In the middle of the cake
exercise: Which sentence uses among to mean being one of a group? | The mouse ran under the grass. | Sam shared the sweets among three friends. | *Humans are among the best long-distance runners of all animals. | A house among the trees stood on the hill.
test: «Parrots are among the cleverest birds.» What does among mean here? | *Being one of a group | Inside a nest | Shared out between people | Far away from
test: A bag of 20 marbles is shared among 4 children. How many marbles does each child get? | 4 | 16 | *5 | 24
exam: What does among mean in «a house among the trees»? | Shared between two people | Far away from the trees | Being the tallest tree | *In the middle of a group
